  "title": "EEG Motor Movement/Imagery Dataset",
  "description": "This dataset comprises over 1500 EEG recordings from 109 volunteers performing motor execution and motor imagery tasks. Subjects performed 14 experimental runs including baseline recordings (eyes open/closed) and four motor tasks involving actual or imagined movement of the fists and feet, recorded using 64-channel EEG with the BCI2000 system. The dataset is designed to support brain-computer interface research and motor imagery classification studies.",
  "methods_description": "EEG data were recorded from 109 subjects using a 64-channel BCI2000 system. Each subject completed 14 experimental runs consisting of two one-minute baseline runs (eyes open and eyes closed) and three two-minute runs each of four motor tasks: (1) actual left/right fist movement, (2) imagined left/right fist movement, (3) actual bilateral fist or foot movement, and (4) imagined bilateral fist or foot movement.",
